diff --git a/util/coroutine-jspi.c b/util/coroutine-jspi.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5469481
--- /dev/null
+++ b/util/coroutine-jspi.c
@@ -0,0 +1,201 @@
+/*
+ * JSPI coroutine backend for Emscripten
+ *
+ * Each coroutine runs on its own WebAssembly stack, created through
+ * WebAssembly.promising(). A switch parks the running stack on a promise by
+ * calling a suspending import (JavaScript Promise Integration), and resumes
+ * the other stack by resolving the promise it is parked on. Nothing is
+ * unwound or rewound: the engine keeps a parked stack as it is, so no
+ * function needs Asyncify instrumentation. The program has to be linked
+ * with -sJSPI, and compiled with -sSUPPORT_LONGJMP=wasm, because only
+ * WebAssembly frames may sit between a stack's entry and the suspend, and
+ * the JavaScript-based setjmp puts a JavaScript frame under cpu_exec.
+ *
+ * What the engine does not switch is the C shadow stack in linear memory,
+ * so every coroutine still owns one, and the switch saves and restores the
+ * stack pointer around the park, the way the fiber backend does.
+ *
+ * A parked coroutine can only be resumed on the thread that parked it, since
+ * the promise lives in that worker. Without iothreads QEMU keeps a coroutine
+ * on the thread that runs its AioContext; a resume from anywhere else stops
+ * with a message rather than corrupting anything.
+ *
